Fixed: in -p and piped runs, the 💡 API-error hints now name --provider / --model instead of REPL slash commands. The REPL hints are unchanged, word for word. fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test suite all pass. Committed as b10ec5d2, titled "Fixes #1128".

What I found
• Hints: I went through every message diagnose_api_error can produce. 3 of its 8 branches suggested a slash command:
  • Billing/quota: /provider <name> and /model ollama/llama3. In a one-shot run these now read --provider <name> and --provider ollama --model llama3.2.
  • Model not found: Switch with: /model X or --model X. This now reads Switch with: --model X.
  • Network: /retry. #1115 already removed this one.
• Call sites: src/prompt.rs prints 💡 hints in five places, and only two adjusted them for one-shot runs. The other three called the plain function, so in -p mode they skipped even #1115's /retry removal. These were the non-retriable error, the rejected-input case and stream-json. All five now go through surface_diagnosis, and the code still checks only one "is this a one-shot run?" flag.

How it's built
• diagnose_api_error_for(error, model, oneshot) is now the pure function, so tests can drive both surfaces directly.
• The hint text lives in src/prompt/network_error_summary.rs.
• The old two-argument diagnose_api_error is now test-only, so every production call site has to pick a surface.
• Neither size-capped file grew: prompt_retry.rs went from 2793 to 2792 lines (I lowered its limit in tests/module_size.rs to match), and prompt.rs stayed at 3937.

Tests
• Both surfaces are tested on the full hint text:
  • REPL billing and model-switch hints must match the old text exactly.
  • One-shot hints must match the new text.
  • Across 7 error types, no one-shot hint contains a slash command. The REPL hint still has one for the 3 that did before, which proves the check can fail.
• As a sanity check, I broke the new one-shot wording on purpose. Exactly the 3 one-shot tests failed, and all 14 passed again once I put it back.
• Real run: I ran the built binary in -p mode against a throwaway Python server, since nothing in tests/ returns a billing or model-not-found error.
  • A 402 "insufficient_quota" response showed --provider <name> and --provider ollama --model llama3.2.
  • A 404 "model not found" response showed Switch with: --model gpt-5.
  • Both exited with code 1.

No docs quote these hints, so nothing there needed changing.

Filed as #1139: the REPL's /model ollama/llama3 advice is also wrong. Reading src/dispatch.rs:747, /model sets that whole string as the model id and keeps the provider that just ran out of credits, so the next call would fail too. #1128 required the REPL wording to stay unchanged, so I left it out of this fix.
